now as 2021 draws to a close i think  we're all getting ready for christmas  but i want to take a bit of an  opportunity just to talk through some of  the highlights of this year  and some of the activities and actions  that we've been taking as a council to  support our residents and businesses  now back in january we announced that  charlie park leisure center and the  sports hall there was going to be used  as part of the vaccination rollout for  coronavirus  and over the course of the year over the  following months  we supported the nhs to deliver 60 000  vaccinations from that centre and i'm  really pleased that the dart north east  alberta district council has been  recognized for its contribution to that  fantastic vaccine rollout over the  course of the year  and then in february we announced that  we were investing in our environmental  health service both in terms of helping  with the public health response to covid  but also to help us deal with issues  like fly tipping and environmental crime  and that's been a fantastic achievement  to be able to expand that service and  really get into some of those difficult  issues that we face  in our rural districts in march we have  an absolutely fantastic month in terms  of government funding for this district  firstly we have the amazing announcement  of 24.1 million pounds for clay cross as  part of the clay crosstown deal  then we also found out we'd have been  awarded 1.6 million pounds  which we've topped up with council the  council's own funding to help us deliver  external wall insulation to over 400  properties around the district and  particularly those hard to heat homes  and then finally we also received a one  million pound gram from the government  to help us improve eckington leisure  centre and make it one of the most  greenest  and most environmentally friendly  leisure centres in the whole of the  region and that works almost due for  completion and hopefully will be  reopened as a pool  very very soon now in april we elected  our 35th chairman of the council  councillor martin bakker and he launched  his  fundraising campaign for ashke hospice  care and since then he's done an  absolute  smattering of events throughout the year  and some fantastic fundraising  activities to raise vital funds for  ashgate hospice care  now in may we held some a very difficult  set of elections because of code  restrictions but fortunately they ran  very very smoothly and we had lots of  positive feedback from residents about  the whole process of voting and all the  mitigations that we put in place to help  make voting and that key part of  being a democratic country possible  during the month of may and then in june  we worked with the government to support  the kickstart scheme to help  give more young people really valuable  experience in work  now in july we signed the contract with  kilimanja parish council as part of our  1.9 million takeover and refurbishment  of the sports centre there now works  already started and i'm really looking  forward to that that centre reopening in  the next few months  and then also in the summer we had some  fantastic awards for some of our  services our health and safety team were  awarded the gold roster award and our  street scene team were also awarded an  apse award for excellent services so  well done to both of those teams  now in september we launched together  with the other districts and county  councils across derbyshire we launched  our vision derbyshire  business grants and advice to businesses  now in october we became the first  council in derbyshire to implement  mandatory cctv  for taxis and private hire vehicles now  we think that will help make both the  passengers and the drivers themselves  safer and we're really proud to have  been the first council to have done that  and also throughout october we did a  series of meet the council events and  also our armed forces covenant event to  celebrate the fantastic work of the  armed forces in november we delivered a  jobs fair in clay cross to help local  people  find local jobs and also our  environmental health team and did a  fantastic job in seizing and crushing a  vehicle  that was known to have been involved in  fly tipping in this area well done to  them  and this month december we've announced  our involvement in the queen's green  canopy scheme which involves planting  trees to help mark the queen's platinum  jubilee next year we're really excited  to be part of this amazing project  and that's just to name a few there's  plenty more on our website and on our  social media channels so please do check  them out and find out more about the  fantastic things that we've been we've  been doing throughout this year  now i know that this time at the moment  is a particularly anxious time for some  people with the concerns around the  omicron variant  and the government's move to plan b but  i think it's absolutely vital that we  all continue to work together  to follow the guidance and follow those  restrictions where necessary and also  make sure that we all get our  vaccinations done and go for our  boosters when we're called to do so we  can continue to work together and i'm  sure we can defeat  the virus and continue to enjoy a good  christmas together all the same and i  hope everyone has a fantastic christmas  and a very happy new year and look  forward to 202 when i'm sure there's a  lot more things we can do as a council  working with our residents and our  businesses and our community groups and  parish councils thank you very much  you
 

